# Profile: REMOTE  —  loaded by `npm run dev:remote`
#
# Local dev server (localhost:5173) talking to the DEPLOYED backend. Useful for
# reproducing a production bug against real data without deploying the frontend.
#
# Two things must be true on the backend for this to work, because the requests are
# now cross-site:
#   1. FRONTEND_ORIGIN on Heroku must include http://localhost:5173
#   2. NODE_ENV=production on Heroku, so the refresh cookie is sent with
#      SameSite=None; Secure (see buildRefreshCookie in backend/index.js)
#
# Note this points at the real production database. Treat writes accordingly.
VITE_BACKEND_BASE=https://chitter-backend-app-4c5e1318fbab.herokuapp.com
